Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.20,0:00:02.45,Midnight,,0,0,0,,Elias's newspaper\Nwas dated tomorrow.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.87,0:00:03.66,Midnight,,0,0,0,,He lived alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.77,0:00:04.88,Midnight,,0,0,0,,He had no subscription.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.32,0:00:05.84,Midnight,,0,0,0,,A misprint —
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.84,0:00:08.52,Midnight,,0,0,0,,until page nine\Nreported his death.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.83,0:00:09.70,Midnight,,0,0,0,,Apartment fire.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.70,0:00:11.86,Midnight,,0,0,0,,Friday. Three a.m.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.86,0:00:12.51,Midnight,,0,0,0,,His name.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.78,0:00:14.53,Midnight,,0,0,0,,He booked a hotel across town.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.96,0:00:17.13,Midnight,,0,0,0,,Saturday's paper was\Nat the front desk.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.57,0:00:18.94,Midnight,,0,0,0,,The fire happened anyway.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.17,0:00:19.88,Midnight,,0,0,0,,Same building.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.03,0:00:20.82,Midnight,,0,0,0,,Same hour.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.87,0:00:21.98,Midnight,,0,0,0,,Different man.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.99,0:00:24.04,Midnight,,0,0,0,,The dead man was\Nhis neighbour, who'd
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.04,0:00:25.28,Midnight,,0,0,0,,knocked to warn him.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.51,0:00:28.00,Midnight,,0,0,0,,Elias spread every\Npaper he'd saved across
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.00,0:00:28.78,Midnight,,0,0,0,,the floor.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.13,0:00:30.16,Midnight,,0,0,0,,All dated tomorrow.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.39,0:00:32.40,Midnight,,0,0,0,,Each mentioned him\Nless than the last.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.92,0:00:33.95,Midnight,,0,0,0,,First his job.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.10,0:00:34.77,Midnight,,0,0,0,,Then his friends.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.77,0:00:36.23,Midnight,,0,0,0,,Then the crossword.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.51,0:00:38.86,Midnight,,0,0,0,,By Friday, his\Nphotograph was a grey
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.86,0:00:41.97,Midnight,,0,0,0,,rectangle. Saturday's\Npaper arrived blank.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.18,0:00:43.71,Midnight,,0,0,0,,Only the masthead remained.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.21,0:00:46.72,Midnight,,0,0,0,,The Midnight Archive:\Nall the news that
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.72,0:00:47.50,Midnight,,0,0,0,,never was.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.00,0:00:49.71,Midnight,,0,0,0,,Elias finally understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.71,0:00:51.97,Midnight,,0,0,0,,It wasn't predicting his future.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.31,0:00:53.78,Midnight,,0,0,0,,It was deciding what to keep.
